Subject: [PATCH] [M159] [editing] Skip pseudo-elements in
 `AbstractLineBox::PositionForPoint`

Original change's description:
> [editing] Skip pseudo-elements in `AbstractLineBox::PositionForPoint`
>
> `AbstractLineBox::CanBeCaretContainer()` skips lines that only contain
> pseudo-elements, but `AbstractLineBox::PositionForPoint()` did not skip
> pseudo-element inline leaves when a line also contains real DOM nodes.
> As a result, vertical line navigation (`NextLinePosition` and
> `PreviousLinePosition`) could anchor a `PositionInFlatTree` at a
> pseudo-element (such as an inline-block `::before`/`::after` or
> `::view-transition`), which violates selection/DOM invariants.
>
> Skip inline leaves without `NonPseudoNode()` in
> `AbstractLineBox::PositionForPoint()` and resolve the closest leaf's
> node via `NonPseudoNode()`.
>
> Fixed: 589812279
